        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lori Swanson, G. Aaron Youngquist, Al Capone\n- Places: Eagan, Dakota County, Minnesota, United States\n- Roles: Minnesota Attorney General, Assistant U.S. Attorney General\n- Events: Minnesota Attorney General election, 2010\n- Organizations: Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party\n\nFacts:\n- G. Aaron Youngquist served as Minnesota Attorney General.\n- G. Aaron Youngquist also served as an Assistant U.S. Attorney General who successfully prosecuted Al Capone for federal income tax evasion.\n- Lori Swanson was born on December 16, 1966.\n- Lori Swanson is from Eagan, Minnesota.\n- Eagan is a city in Dakota County, Minnesota, United States.\n- Lori Swanson is the Attorney General of the U.S. state of Minnesota.\n- In the 2010 Minnesota Attorney General election, incumbent Lori Swanson of the Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party won reelection to a second term.",
